# The build context is the repo root, and most of the repo has no business in
# it. Two entries below are not size optimisations but licensing ones.

# Build output. `target/` alone is several GB and would dominate the upload.
target/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# M6.5b2's help-panel INTERMEDIATES. `shots.spec.ts` writes PNG here because
# Playwright has no WebP encoder, and `docs/tools/mkhelpart.py` cuts the
# committed `web/public/help/*.webp` from them. 4.2 MB of input to a step this
# build never runs — and MEASURED in the image before this line existed, which
# is the same way the two lines below were found.
web/help-shots/

# M6.5b's generated glue, both targets. These are BUILD OUTPUT of
# `npm run build:wasm` and are gitignored — but a .gitignore governs git and
# not a build context, so without these two lines a developer's own module
# rides into the image. The `client` stage's `COPY --from=server /out/wasm`
# would then be overwriting a stale copy rather than delivering the only one,
# and `wasm-node/` (which no stage wants) would ship in the client layer.
# Measured: both were in the context before these lines existed.
web/src/local/wasm/
web/wasm-node/

# **Third-party material that must not enter an image that gets pushed
# anywhere.** `ASSETS.md` carves these out of the Apache-2.0 grant, and pushing
# them to a registry is redistribution. `crates/yokohama-web/assets/art/` is the
# deliberate exception — the running client draws it, so it is COPYed in
# explicitly by the Dockerfile — and that makes the resulting image itself
# carved-out material. Do not push this image to a public registry.
tts-assets/
analysis-1/

# Captures, corpora and local research. Gitignored or not, none of it is input
# to a build.
bridge-captures/
docs/temp/
.claude/
.agents/
.codex/
.vscode/

# **Secrets and sessions never enter a build context** (security S2a, finding D15) — under BuildKit, which reads
# this file as `deploy/Dockerfile`'s own ignore (the legacy builder reads none; Docker 23 builds with BuildKit by
# default). `.dev.vars` is wrangler's file of credentials (the repository root holds one) and `.env*` is Vite's;
# either may sit in any directory of the context — web/, worker/, the root — so the patterns are `**/`: anchored
# at the root they would exclude the root's alone (measured: `web/.env*` and `worker/.dev.vars` entered the
# context). `web/scripts/pinned/` is the pinned-browser instrument's state, whose Chromium profiles held the
# deployment's Access session cookie, and `COPY web/ ./` in the client stage would have carried it into the image's
# layers. A .gitignore governs git, not a build context.
**/.dev.vars
**/.dev.vars.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
web/scripts/pinned/

# History and tooling.
.git/
.github/
*.md
!README.md

# The BGA bridge's browser half and its node suites: a separate product that
# shares the repo and nothing else.
bridge/

# **Tests, out of the image build — and this is correctness, not tidiness.**
# The client stage's build script is `build:client`, i.e. `tsc -b && vite
# build`, and `tsconfig.json` includes all of `src`, so a type error in any
# *.test.tsx FAILS THE PRODUCTION IMAGE.
# Caught the honest way: a stray probe file left in the tree by another process
# broke this build with three TS6133 unused-variable errors in a file the
# bundle never imports. The test suites are CI's job and the per-edit gates';
# an image build should depend on the code it ships and nothing else.
web/src/**/*.test.ts
web/src/**/*.test.tsx
web/src/test/
web/e2e/
web/playwright.config.ts
web/vitest.config.ts

# Rust tests and examples travel with their crates (cargo needs the manifests
# to agree), so they are NOT excluded here — `cargo build --release -p
# yokohama-web` simply does not compile them.

# Belt and braces: `**` semantics differ between ignore implementations,
# so the single-level case is spelled out rather than assumed.
web/src/*.test.ts
web/src/*.test.tsx
